From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:11:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LinuxEmulation: room for a large self-modifying program's SMC
 hot pages

The SMC hot set (SMCHotPageTracker) held at most 1,536 pages (3/4 of 2,048
slots). Age of Empires II DE writes to ~2,900 of its code pages over and
over; the 1,625 pages that could never become hot took 82% of its 228k
write faults, each one an invalidation and a re-translation. The hot set
now has 32,768 slots and the fault counters 65,536 (768 KiB per process).

In the game's first 60 s: SMC faults 920k -> 131k, signal time 32 s -> 6 s;
its main menu 57 s -> 50 s after launch (8 launches in 8).

fex-tests jit-capacity: 2,048 code pages written next to their running
code take 32 faults each (116,224 before).
---
 Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SMCHotPages.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SMCHotPages.h b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SMCHotPages.h
index d46b7ea..3d3c471 100644
--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SMCHotPages.h
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/SMCHotPages.h
@@ -79,8 +79,10 @@ public:
   }
 
 private:
-  static constexpr size_t CounterSlots = 4096;
-  static constexpr size_t HotSlots = 2048;
+  // Sized for a large protected executable: Age of Empires II DE writes to ~2,900 of its code pages over and over, and
+  // with 2,048 hot slots (1,536 usable) the pages left out took 82% of its faults. 768 KiB per process.
+  static constexpr size_t CounterSlots = 65536;
+  static constexpr size_t HotSlots = 32768;
   static constexpr unsigned CountBits = 20;
   static constexpr uint64_t CountMask = (1ULL << CountBits) - 1;
   static_assert((CounterSlots & (CounterSlots - 1)) == 0 && (HotSlots & (HotSlots - 1)) == 0);
